    "original-info": "In September 1812 went to Lisbon as Clerk in the Commissariat Department of the Duke of Wellington's Army. Arrived in Hobart Town in 1824. In 1842 placed on the Commission of the Peace and remained a magistrate until his death, a period of 30 years. Received a large grant of land as a military officer but never settled on it. Built a residence at New Town where he died. Married the , barrister and Chairman of Quarter Sessions. 21 Oct 1872 Supreme Court of Tasmania, will of William Fletcher proved, administration to George William Fletcher son and sole executor",
